**Definition 10.1 (The normalized pure source).** Continue [Probability, Phase Transport and Holonomy][T10] after its
chapter 9. Fix one normalized full-support pure source with
mode order $(0,1,2,3,13)$ and write

$$
X=p_1+p_{13},\qquad Y=p_3+p_{13},\qquad Z=p_2,
\qquad r=1-Z,\qquad \kappa=p_{13}.
$$

The affine fiber is

$$
p(\kappa)=(r-X-Y+\kappa,\ X-\kappa,\ Z,\ Y-\kappa,\ \kappa),
$$

where

$$
J_b=(\ell_b,u_b),\quad
\ell_b=\max(0,X+Y-r),\quad u_b=\min(X,Y),\quad
Z>0,\quad \ell_b<u_b.
$$

Thus $p_s>0$ throughout the declared open fiber. A pure representative is

$$
\psi_s=\sqrt{p_s}\,e^{-i\theta_s},
\qquad C_{ij}=\overline{\psi_i}\psi_j.
\tag{10.1}
$$

The native menu is

$$
E=\{01,02,03,1\!\text{--}\!13,3\!\text{--}\!13\}.
$$

Its reported pair is the original $(2\operatorname{Re}C_{ij},
2\operatorname{Im}C_{ij})$, including the factor two and the displayed
orientation. The probability-mean kernel is generated by
$d=(1,-1,0,-1,1)$; the logarithmic coherence kernel is a different
object, so a null direction for means is not automatically a phase-null
direction.

